	(text "NIBBLE CARD CTR4 - COUNTER BIT 4: program counter bit 4 and return register bit 4"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.4 15.24 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 3.5 3.5)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "6ada8cb1-4f5e-4847-b1ba-b5b63c094407")
	)
	(text "Cell: 2N7000 + 47k pull-up (NMOS, see docs/gate-cell.md).  62 transistors, 34 resistors, 2 LEDs, 100 x 100 mm (docs/cards.md).\nFrom the bus header: PCE (count), PCL (load the jump target), CLK, RST.   To the bus header: PC4.\nFrom the sequencer over the LINK ribbon (2x6, chained along the eight counter cards): OPR4 (the jump target bit), PCR (load the return address), RAI (save the return address).\nCount carry TC4 in from bit 3 over the IN link; TC5 = TC4 and PC4 out to bit 5 over the OUT link.\nPC4: a master-slave flip-flop whose input is PC xor carry (count, or hold when PCE is low), OPR4 (PCL) or RA4 (PCR).  RA4: a transparent latch open while RAI and PH1.  RST clears both.\ndocs/isa.md is the specification; sim/emu.py the reference the whole-machine simulation checks the cards against."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.4 45.72 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.6 1.6)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "78cf6eb0-a2d1-40d0-ad9c-e93601db5ec2")
	)
	(text "TWO-PHASE CLOCK and RSTN (as on the register and sequencer boards)"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.4 165.1 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2 2)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "cd1081e7-70fd-4b4c-baa7-b3d8e54ad1c7")
	)
